.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt VMNOTIFY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vmnotify
.Nd forward Windows VM notifications to the Linux desktop
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm vmnotify
.Op Fl dhVv
.Op Fl b Ar x,y,w,h
.Op Fl c Ar sec
.Op Fl i Ar sec
.Op Fl m Ar regex
.Op Fl s Ar file
.Op Fl t Ar x,y,w,h
.Op Ar server
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the screen of a VMware Workstation virtual machine through the VNC
server built into VMware and turns Windows notifications into desktop
notifications on the host.
Nothing runs inside the guest.
.Pp
Unless set, the toast area and the taskbar are found on the first full
update of the screen.
Going up from the bottom of the screen, the first row under which most
pixels change colour, between 24 and 160 rows up, is the top of the
taskbar: its border, or the edge to what is above it.
Without one, as when the taskbar is hidden, it is taken as 48 rows, its
height at 100% display scaling.
The toast area is 420 by 380 pixels in the right corner just above the
taskbar, larger in proportion when the taskbar is higher than 48 rows, at
a larger display scaling.
After that, only changes in the box covering the toast area and the
taskbar are requested from the VNC server, which sends them as they
happen.
The whole area is requested again after the screen size changed.
When the toast area changed and then stayed the same for the time set
with
.Fl i ,
which skips the slide in animation of toasts, it is compared with how it
looked without a toast, ignoring small colour shifts.
Unless a toast is already on screen, the change is only read when it
covers at least 15% of the area or spans at least 40 rows, about two
lines of text, so that a line changing in a window underneath does not
cost a recognition.
Only the changed part is read: the solid rectangle a toast paints when
its background differs from what is underneath, or else all changed
pixels.
For a solid rectangle, changes more than 24 blank rows away from it,
such as a line changing higher up in a window underneath, are left out,
unless nothing to forward is read in it: it may be a window opening at
the same time as a toast.
It is converted to grey, light text on a dark background is turned dark
on light, it is scaled up twice and passed to
.Xr tesseract 1 .
When the area is back to how it looked before the toast, the toast is
gone and nothing is read.
The area is also read once at start, so a toast already on screen is
forwarded.
If the recognised text matches
.Ar regex ,
its first line is sent as summary and the remaining lines as body in a
desktop notification, over D-Bus.
Every summary starts with the name of the machine it comes from, so that
several
.Nm
can be told apart: the desktop name the VNC server gives, or else the
server address.
The same text is only sent once while it stays on screen.
Lines are compared by their ASCII letters and digits, ignoring case,
and count as the same when at most a quarter of them differs, so that
stray characters read from an icon, or from a button appearing when the
mouse is over the toast, do not make it new.
When a new toast stacks with one already sent, both are read and only
the lines of the new one are sent, if they match
.Ar regex .
The same goes for a new toast taking the place of one that went away
at the same time, as when Windows shows a queued toast.
When one of a stack goes away, nothing is sent.
.Pp
The taskbar is watched as well, for badges in the corner of app icons.
Teams draws its own, green, yellow or grey with your presence and red
with a white mark or count on new activity, also when no toast is
shown, as for a message in the chat already open.
These colours are the same whatever the theme.
Windows draws the badges apps ask it for, such as the envelope Outlook
shows for new mail, as a disc filled with the accent colour, a single
colour where icons are shaded.
When the clearly red pixels of the taskbar grow by at least 40, a
.Dq Red badge on the taskbar icon
notification is sent.
When those of single colour areas narrower than a badge do, a
.Dq New badge on the taskbar icon
notification is sent.
Its summary names the app when its icon, next to the pixels turning red
or of a single colour, looks like one of Microsoft Teams, Outlook,
Slack, WhatsApp, Signal or Telegram; it is
.Dq VM
otherwise.
Badges going away, presence changes, the mouse over an icon, icons
moving along the taskbar and all of it coming back, as after the lock
screen or a full screen window, send nothing, and neither do badges
already there at start.
.Pp
With
.Cm checkupdates yes
in
.Pa ~/.vmnotifyrc ,
.Nm
asks GitHub at start with
.Xr curl 1
which release is the latest and says so when it is newer.
Nothing is said when curl is missing or GitHub out of reach, which it is
given 5 seconds for.
Nothing is asked by default.
.Pp
Only one
.Nm
watches at a time, a second one exits with an error.
Taking a screenshot with
.Fl s
is always possible.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar x,y,w,h
Watch the
.Ar w
by
.Ar h
pixels at
.Ar x , Ns Ar y
for badges instead of the taskbar, or with
.Cm none
nothing.
.It Fl c Ar sec
Send no other badge notification for
.Ar sec
seconds after one.
The default is 30, the maximum 86400.
.It Fl d
Run in the background and log to
.Xr syslog 3 .
Whenever watching stops on an error, for example because the virtual
machine is powered off or the password is wrong, or cannot start because
the process limit is reached, it starts again after 30 seconds.
The process starting it again shows as
.Dq vmnotify: monitor
in
.Xr ps 1 ,
followed by the server, the one watching as
.Dq vmnotify: watcher ,
followed by the machine name and the server, and its helper as
.Dq vmnotify: helper ,
followed by the server, see
.Sx SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS .
.It Fl h
Show the version and a summary of the options and of
.Pa ~/.vmnotifyrc ,
then exit.
.It Fl i Ar sec
Read the toast area once it did not change for
.Ar sec
seconds.
The default is 1, the maximum 3600.
.It Fl m Ar regex
Only forward toasts whose text matches the case insensitive extended
regular expression
.Ar regex .
The default is
.Ql teams|outlook|firefox .
.It Fl s Ar file
Save the guest screen to
.Ar file
as a binary PPM image and exit.
A new file is only readable by the user.
It is made before connecting, see
.Sx SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS ,
and left empty when the screenshot cannot be taken.
This helps to find the coordinates for
.Fl b
and
.Fl t .
.It Fl t Ar x,y,w,h
The toast area, instead of the one found above the taskbar.
At 100% display scaling, that is
.Ql -420,-430,420,380 .
.It Fl V
Log every step with a timestamp on standard error, or with
.Fl d
to
.Xr syslog 3 :
the settings in use, the VNC protocol exchange, the native pixel format
of the server, every update request and update received, every run of
.Xr tesseract 1
and every notification sent.
The password and the authentication challenge and response are never
logged.
Implies
.Fl v .
.It Fl v
Print the text read from the toast area and badges on
standard output, or with
.Fl d
to
.Xr syslog 3 .
.El
.Pp
In regions, a negative
.Ar x
or
.Ar y
counts from the right or bottom edge of the screen.
Regions are at most 4096 by 4096 pixels.
.Pp
Guest screens larger than 8192 pixels on either side are not supported.
.Pp
.Ar server
is
.Ar host ,
.Ar host : Ns Ar display
or
.Ar host :: Ns Ar port .
An IPv6 address is written in brackets.
The default is
.Ql 127.0.0.1::5900 .
.Pp
Only the RFB security types None and VNC authentication are supported,
which is what VMware Workstation offers.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
.It Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The D-Bus session bus notifications are sent on, as set by the desktop.
Its first
.Ql unix:path=
or
.Ql unix:abstract=
address that can be reached is used.
When it is not set,
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus .
.It Ev HOME
Where
.Pa .vmnotifyrc
is read from, and where the lock file goes when
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set.
.It Ev VNC_PASSWORD
Password for the VNC server, used instead of the one in
.Pa ~/.vmnotifyrc .
It is removed from the environment of the commands
.Nm
runs.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for the lock file, and for the session bus when
.Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
is not set.
.El
.Pp
.Ev OMP_THREAD_LIMIT
is set to 1 for
.Xr tesseract 1 ,
whose threads make recognising a small image much slower.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.vmnotifyrc
Settings, one
.Dq Ar keyword value
per line.
Empty lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored, as are blanks around the value.
A later line for the same keyword replaces an earlier one, and command
line options take precedence over the file.
The file must be owned by the user and not be accessible by anyone else.
The keywords are:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "password secret" -compact
.It Cm password Ar secret
Password for the VNC server.
.It Cm match Ar regex
Like
.Fl m .
.It Cm server Ar server
Like the
.Ar server
argument.
.It Cm toast Ar x,y,w,h
Like
.Fl t .
.It Cm badge Ar x,y,w,h | Cm none
Like
.Fl b .
.It Cm interval Ar sec
Like
.Fl i .
.It Cm cooldown Ar sec
Like
.Fl c .
.It Cm checkupdates Cm yes | Cm no
Whether to say at start when a newer release is out, asking GitHub.
The default is
.Cm no .
.El
.It Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vmnotify.lock
Locked while
.Nm
watches, holds its process ID.
.Pa ~/.vmnotify.lock
is used when
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 after
.Fl h
or
.Fl s
and 1 on error.
Without
.Fl d ,
that includes the connection to the VNC server failing or being closed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A
.Pa ~/.vmnotifyrc
forwarding Teams and Outlook only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
password secret
match teams|outlook
.Ed
.Pp
Create it with the right permissions first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ install -m 600 /dev/null ~/.vmnotifyrc
.Ed
.Pp
Find the regions on a screenshot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vmnotify -s shot.ppm
.Ed
.Pp
Check what is read, then run in the background:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vmnotify -v
$ vmnotify -d
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr tesseract 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Renaud Allard Aq Mt renaud@allard.it
.Sh CAVEATS
The VNC server of VMware Workstation may listen on all addresses.
Anyone who can reach it can see and control the virtual machine, so the
port should be blocked in the host firewall.
.Pp
A toast is only read once the toast area stopped changing for the time
set with
.Fl i .
If something keeps changing behind a translucent toast, such as a video,
it is not read.
.Pp
A toast that is not forwarded and then replaced by one that is, with
only its first line differing, is not read.
When a toast below others is dismissed while a queued one appears, the
toasts still on screen are sent again with the new one.
App icons and close buttons may add a few stray characters to the text.
.Pp
A window underneath whose content moves right next to the toast as it
appears, such as a list of mails getting a new one, may add some of its
text to the notification.
.Pp
Any window in the toast area whose text matches
.Ar regex
triggers a notification.
.Pp
Teams also makes its badge red when your presence is busy or do not
disturb, as at the start of a meeting, which sends a red badge
notification.
.Pp
An app starting whose icon was not on the taskbar yet sends a red or
new badge notification when the icon has red areas or areas of a single
colour, as those of Acrobat, YouTube, Office, Gmail, Signal or Spotify
do.
On Windows 10, so may a progress bar on an icon or a flashing one.
The badge of the Widgets button sends a red or new badge notification named
.Dq VM .
.Pp
Badges appearing at once on icons further apart than the taskbar is
thick are not reported.
.Pp
The taskbar is only looked for at the bottom of the screen, and only at
start: a taskbar on another edge, hidden at start, or a display scaling
changed later needs the regions set.
Apps are only named on a taskbar at the top or bottom.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Everything the VNC server sends, the guest screen included, is read by
the watching process, or with
.Fl s ,
under a seccomp filter, set right after connecting.
It may only read and write what it has open, wait for it, handle its
memory, never made executable, and tell the time.
Opening files, creating sockets and
.Xr ioctl 2
fail; any other system call ends it, and with
.Fl d
the restart is logged as such.
.Pp
Running
.Xr tesseract 1
and sending notifications over D-Bus need much more, and tesseract
would inherit the filter.
A helper process, forked before the filter is set and shown as
.Dq vmnotify: helper ,
does both for the watcher, over a socket pair, and checks what it is
asked.
The filter is not used in builds with sanitizers, which make system calls
of their own, nor on other architectures than amd64 and arm64.
Builds with gcc before 14 and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer alone need
.Fl DNOSECCOMP .
